WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.767
The same table can support several aggregate
measures in one query This

00:00:05.794 --> 00:00:11.254
example summarizes sales using functions such as SUM
AVG MIN and MAX

00:00:12.191 --> 00:00:17.244
Before running it make a prediction The total
quantity and total revenue

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:21.046
answer different questions while the minimum and
maximum show the range of

00:00:21.073 --> 00:00:26.891
individual values Run the query in the browser and
inspect each result

00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:31.880
column Notice that PostgreSQL can calculate all of
these measures from the

00:00:31.894 --> 00:00:36.928
same set of source rows The important idea is not to
add

00:00:36.941 --> 00:00:41.694
every aggregate function just because you can Choose
measures that support the

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:47.089
analytical question A decision-maker usually needs a
small set of clearly named

00:00:47.115 --> 00:00:49.470
metrics rather than every possible summary
